This is the best general way to get posterior samples from a derived quantity. One of us (maybe me?) should probably add this to the documentation for tmbstan. In your simple example if it's a straight function of parameters you can just apply that function to the posterior samples and get a posterior for that function. For more complicated things you'll want to use the report() solution above. -Cole

